14 Termination and Cure
Your rights automatically suspend upon material breach. If the breach is curable, is Your first 
material breach and is not intentional commercial exploitation, impersonation, fraud, deliberate 
circumvention of access controls or credential misuse, Your rights automatically reinstate if You 
fully cure within 30 days after written notice from Licensor. If You do not timely cure, Your rights 
automatically terminate at the end of that cure period. An ineligible breach causes termination 
upon Licensor's written notice. Other reinstatement requires Licensor's signed writing.
A notice under this section may be sent by email to an address You supplied to Licensor or publicly 
designate for legal or account notices, through a relevant account or repository notice reasonably 
calculated to reach You, or by another method permitted by law. Notice is effective when 
transmitted unless applicable law requires otherwise. If Licensor has no reasonably available 
address, suspension continues, but a curable breach does not terminate under this section until 
written notice is sent.
After termination, cease all use, modification and distribution requiring permission and remove 
publicly distributed copies under Your control where reasonably practicable. You may keep one 
archival copy if law requires it. Recipients who obtained copies while You complied retain their 
rights while they remain compliant. Ownership, trademark, service-boundary, disclaimer, liability, 
governing-law and naturally surviving provisions survive.
